     "id": "T1",
     "type": "mc",
     "text": "The slope of the secant line through $(a, f(a))$ and $(b, f(b))$ is",
     "options": [
      "$frac{f(b) - f(a)}{b - a}$",
      "$frac{b - a}{f(b) - f(a)}$",
      "$frac{f(b) + f(a)}{b + a}$",
      "$f(b) - f(a)$"
     ],
     "answer": 0,
     "explain": "Rise over run: change in $y$ over change in $x$."
    },
    {
     "id": "T2",
     "type": "mc",
     "text": "$f'(a)$ is the slope of the",
     "options": [
      "tangent line at $x = a$",
      "secant line from 0 to $a$",
      "graph at its highest point",
      "line through the origin and $(a, f(a))$"
     ],
     "answer": 0,
     "explain": "The derivative at a point is the slope of the tangent line there: how steep the graph is right at $x = a$."
    },
    {
     "id": "T3",
     "type": "tf",
     "text": "To find $f'(a)$, you can just plug $h = 0$ into $frac{f(a+h) - f(a)}{h}$.",
     "answer": false,
     "explain": "That gives $frac{0}{0}$. Simplify first (cancel the $h$), then let $h -> 0$."
    },
    {
     "id": "T4",
     "type": "match",
     "text": "Match each word to what it means.",
     "pairs": [
      [
       "Secant line",
       "meets the curve at two points"
      ],
      [
       "Tangent line",
       "has the slope of the curve at one point"
      ],
      [
       "Derivative $f'(a)$",
       "the slope of the tangent line"
      ],
      [
       "Difference quotient",
       "$frac{f(a+h) - f(a)}{h}$"
      ]
     ],
     "explain": "The difference quotient is a secant slope. Its limit as $h -> 0$ is the derivative."
    },
    {
     "id": "T5",
     "type": "mc",
     "text": "The equation of the tangent line to $f$ at $x = a$ is",
     "options": [
      "$y = f'(a)(x - a) + f(a)$",
      "$y = f(a)(x - a) + f'(a)$",
      "$y = f'(x)(x - a)$",
      "$y = f'(a)x$"
     ],
     "answer": 0,
     "explain": "Point-slope form with slope $f'(a)$ through the point $(a, f(a))$."
    },
    {
     "id": "T6",
     "type": "mc",
     "text": "Which limit is also equal to $f'(a)$?",
     "options": [
      "$lim[x->a] frac{f(x) - f(a)}{x - a}$",
      "$lim[x->a] frac{f(x) + f(a)}{x + a}$",
